{"type":"message","id":"2fcf3c17","parentId":"80fdfe1a","timestamp":"2026-04-17T10:28:28.077Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue might be that the feishu_im_user_message tool doesn't support sending interactive cards directly - it might need a different approach. Let me check the tool description again.Actually, looking at the tool description for feishu_im_user_message:\n- msg_type: text, post, image, file, audio, media, interactive, share_chat, share_user\n\nSo interactive should be supported. But maybe the issue is with how the content is formatted. Let me try using the exact API format from the docs - the card should be in the `content` field as a JSON string.Actually wait, looking at the API documentation, for sending messages the content should be a string (JSON serialized). But the feishu_im_user_message tool takes a `content` field that is already the content. Maybe the issue is that the tool already handles serialization?Let me try passing just the card object (without wrapping in another object with msg_type):"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0pkyz7rg0hji_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"app_id\": \"cli_a76034a18870d00c\", \"app_secret\": \"'\"$(cat ~/.credentials/feishu_app_secret.txt 2>/dev/null || echo '')\"}'\"}"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776421699259,"responseId":"06313e433a399bce7231c5545c3a30ca"}}
